0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z03-S01","name":"Zone III · Scene 1: City at War — The Besieged Wall & Tall Golden Gods","zone":"Z03","lines":"18.509–519","greek":"Τὴν δ᾽ ἑτέρην πόλιν ἀμφὶ δύω στρατοὶ εἵατο λαῶν τεύχεσι λαμπόμενοι, δίχα δέ σφισιν ἥνδανε βουλή, ἠὲ διαπραθέειν ἢ ἄνδιχα πάντα δάσασθαι... ἦρχε δ᾽ ἄρα σφιν Ἄρης καὶ Παλλὰς Ἀθήνη ἄμφω χρυσείω, χρύσεια δὲ εἵματα ἕσθην, καλὼ καὶ μεγάλω σὺν τεύχεσιν, ὥς τε θεώ περ, ἀμφὶς ἀριζήλω· λαοὶ δ᾽ ὑπ᾽ ὀλίζονες ἦσαν.","buckley":"But around the other city sat two armies of people, glittering in arms; and a plan was agreeable to them, either to destroy it entirely, or to divide all the wealth into two parts, which the pleasant city contained within it. But they did not yet obey, but were secretly arming for an ambush; their beloved wives and young children stood upon the wall guarding it, and together with them the men whom old age possessed. But they advanced; and Mars and Pallas Minerva led them, both golden, and clad in golden garments, beautiful and large with their arms, like gods, both very conspicuous; but the people were smaller.","worldModel":{"vision":"Hieratic scale contrast encoded in LDraw geometry: Ares and Pallas Athena are 11-brick-tall golden colossi while mortal warriors and rampart defenders are 4-brick minifigures.","memory":"Binary strategic fork (sack vs. divide wealth in half) rejected by the besieged, triggering the covert ambush transition.","controller":"Divine war-marshals propelling the mortal sortie out from the Scaean ramparts."}}

